@startuml comm-call-next
' UML communication diagram: "Call next patient" (FR-QUE-06).
' Objects are linked; numbered messages show the order (same interaction as the sequence diagram,
' but emphasising which objects collaborate).
!pragma layout smetana
allowmixing
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam object {
  BackgroundColor #EFFCF9
  BorderColor #088577
}
left to right direction

actor ":Staff member" as Staff
object ":Workspace UI" as UI
object ":Express router" as Router
object ":authenticate / authorize" as Auth
object ":QueueController" as Ctl
object ":QueueService" as Svc
object ":Visit model" as Visit
database "visits\ncollection" as Coll
object "Who's Next display" as Disp

Staff --> UI : 1: click Call next
UI --> Router : 2: POST /api/queue/:stage/call-next
Router --> Auth : 3: verify session & role
Auth --> Ctl : 4: callNext(req)
Ctl --> Svc : 5: callNext(stage, actor)
Svc --> Visit : 6: findOne(busy?)\n7: findOneAndUpdate(waiting → called,\nsort priority, queueTime)
Visit --> Coll : 8: atomic update on one document
Svc --> Ctl : 9: visit | null
Ctl --> UI : 10: 200 {visit}
Disp --> Router : 11: GET /api/public/queue (poll)
@enduml
